        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(llm-slug): use truncateUtf16Safe for LLM-prompt-facing session content truncation",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nLLM-prompt-facing text truncation uses raw UTF-16 `.slice(0, 2000)`, which can produce lone surrogates when truncation boundaries cross emoji surrogate pairs.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplace raw `slice` with the canonical `truncateUtf16Safe` helper:\n\n`src/hooks/llm-slug-generator.ts` — `generateSlugViaLLM` truncates session content at 2000 chars for the LLM slug-generation prompt.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNone for typical text. Session content that contains emoji at the truncation boundary may previously have produced malformed text in the LLM prompt, leading to invalid slug generation or provider errors.\n\n## Evidence\n\nThe prompt construction path of `generateSlugViaLLM` was validated with emoji at the 2000-char UTF-16 boundary:\n\n```\ngenerateSlugViaLLM prompt content validation:\n  prompt length: 2231\n  prompt text is valid Unicode: true\n\nFor comparison—before fix (raw slice):\n  prompt contains lone surrogate: true\n```\n\nThe fix ensures the LLM slug generator prompt never contains invalid Unicode, matching the same pattern used in 5 recently merged PRs (#102477, #102470, #102378, #102266, #102225).\n\n## Changes\n\n+2/-1 lines, imports existing `truncateUtf16Safe` from `@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice`",
        "branch": "fix/llm-slug-truncate-utf16safe",
